<<<
The cresis or watersheds of the Alps & Jura are about eighty miles apart./
===
*The crests or watersheds of the Alps & Jura are about eighty miles apart.*/
>>>

<<<
(Geikie)The watershed of a country or continent is thus a line which divides the flow of the brooks & rivers on two opposite slopes./
===
(Geikie)*The watershed of a country or continent is thus a line which divides the flow of the brooks & rivers on two opposite slopes.*/
>>>

<<<
(Newspaper)The Seine, between its source in the Côte d'Or & the capital, has many tributaries, & when there is bad weather in the watershed of each of these an excessive flow is bound to be the result. waterspout. See WIND, n.
===
(Newspaper)*The Seine, between its source in the Côte d'Or & the capital, has many tributaries, & when there is bad weather in the watershed of each of these an excessive flow is bound to be the result.*

**waterspout.** See ^^WIND^^, n.
>>>

<<<
wave makes -vable, -vy; see MUTE E.
===
**wave** makes *-vable, -vy*; see ^^MUTE E^^.
>>>

<<<
wax. Wax doll, & wax candle; no hyphen; HyPuens 3 B.
===
**wax.** *Wax doll, & wax candle*; no hyphen; ^^HYPHENS^^ 3 B.
>>>

<<<
waxen. See -EN ADJECTIVES.
===
**waxen.** See ^^-EN ADJECTIVES^^.
>>>

<<<
way. 1l. For ‘at the parting of the ways’ see PARTING. 2 Under way (not weigh) is the right phrase for in motion. 3. See one’s way to.
===
**way.** 1. For 'at the parting of the ways' see ^^PARTING^^. 2. *Under way* (not *weigh*) is the right phrase for in motion. 3. *See* one's *way to*.
>>>

<<<
 We hope that the Government will see their way of giving effect to this suggestion. What has happened?
===
 *We hope that the Government will see their way* of giving effect to *this suggestion.* What has happened?
>>>

<<<
but finding himself saying ‘ will see their way to give effect to’ has shied at the two tos; but he ‘should have abandoned instead of mutilating his phrase; see Our OF THE FRYING-PAN, & CAST-IRON IDIOM.
===
but finding himself saying 'will see their way *to* give effect *to*' has shied at the two *to*s; but he should have abandoned instead of mutilating his phrase; see ^^OUT OF THE FRYING-PAN^^, & ^^CAST-IRON IDIOM^^.
>>>

