<<<
wed is a poetic or rhetorical synonym for marry; & the established past & p.p. is wedded; but it is noticeable that the need of brevity in newspaper headings is bringing into trivial use both the verb instead of marry (DUKE WEDS ACTRESS), & the short
===
**wed** is a poetic or rhetorical synonym for *marry*; & the established past & p.p. is *wedded*; but it is noticeable that the need of brevity in newspaper headings is bringing into trivial use both the verb instead of *marry* (^^DUKE WEDS ACTRESS^^), & the short
>>>

<<<
 instead of the long p.p. (SUICIDE OF WED PAIR); see INconcruous VOCABULARY; here is a chance for sub-editors to do the language a service, if they will. For the effect of headlines, cf. WORKLESS.
===
 instead of the long p.p. (^^SUICIDE OF WED PAIR^^); see ^^INCONGRUOUS VOCABULARY^^; here is a chance for sub-editors to do the language a service, if they will. For the effect of headlines, cf. ^^WORKLESS^^.
>>>

